# Pirate Shores Security Lab

A Flask web app I’m building to better understand how web apps work while learning cybersecurity.

## Overview
This project is me learning by building. I’m starting simple, then I’ll be breaking it (SQL injection, brute force, etc) and fixing it so I actually understand how these attacks work.
while learning Python, Flask and HTML.

## Current Features
- Login page with Flask  
- Form input working  
- Uses POST requests  
- Basic username/password check  

## Why I’m doing this
- To actually understand how login systems work  
- To learn cybersecurity by testing things myself  
- To get comfortable with backend logic and how data flows  

## Tech
- Python  
- Flask  
- HTML  

## Progress

### Day 2
- Built the login page  
- Got GET and POST working  
- Added a simple username/password check  

### Day 1
- Set up Flask  
- Made basic routes (`/`, `/data`)  
- Got it running in the browser  
